<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE concept PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA 1.3 Concept//EN" "concept.dtd">
<concept id="t00184">
	<title>Lighting control</title>
	<shortdesc>The light switch has a headlight and a position lamp setting.</shortdesc>
	<prolog>
		<metadata>
			<keywords>
				<indexterm>lighting
					<indexterm>lighting control</indexterm>
				</indexterm>
				<indexterm>lighting control</indexterm>
			</keywords>
		</metadata>
	</prolog>
	<conbody>
		<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e01111">
			<tgroup cols="2" colsep="0" rowsep="1">
				<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<tbody>
					<row rowsep="1">
						<entry colname="col1">
							<fig id="e01112">
								<image href="images/N_SP327_B05_001.jpg" scale="95" align="center" placement="break"/>
							</fig>
						</entry>
						<entry colname="col2">
							<ol outputclass="callout" id="e01113">
								<li>
									<p>Headlamps <term translate="no">ON</term></p>
								</li>
								<li>
									<p>Position lamp and taillight</p>
								</li>
								<li>
									<p><term translate="no">AUTO</term></p>
								</li>
								<li>
									<p><term translate="no">OFF</term></p>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</entry>
					</row>
				</tbody>
			</tgroup>
		</table>
		<p>To operate the lights, turn the knob at the end of the control lever to one of the following settings:</p>
		<section id="e01114">
			<title>Position Lamp &amp; Taillight <image href="images/WKIA_049.jpg" scale="15" align="left" placement="inline"/></title>
			<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e01115">
				<tgroup cols="2" colsep="0" rowsep="1">
					<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
					<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
					<tbody>
						<row rowsep="1">
							<entry colname="col1">
								<fig id="e01116">
									<image href="images/N_SP327_B05_002.jpg" scale="95" align="center" placement="break"/>
								</fig>
							</entry>
							<entry colname="col2"/>
						</row>
					</tbody>
				</tgroup>
			</table>
			<p>When the light switch is in the lamp position, the front position lamp, taillight, and the license plate lamp will turn on.</p>
		</section>
		<section id="e01117">
			<title>Headlight (Low Beam) <image href="images/WKIA_047.jpg" scale="15" align="center" placement="inline"/></title>
			<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e01118">
				<tgroup cols="2" colsep="0" rowsep="1">
					<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
					<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
					<tbody>
						<row rowsep="1">
							<entry colname="col1">
								<fig id="e01119">
									<image align="center" placement="break" scale="95" href="images/N_SP327_B05_003.jpg"/>
								</fig>
							</entry>
							<entry colname="col2"/>
						</row>
					</tbody>
				</tgroup>
			</table>
			<p>When the light switch is in the headlight position, headlight (low beam), taillight and license plate lamp will turn on.</p>
			<note otherprops="Legal_EU_europe_43_001" type="note" id="e01120">
				<ul id="e01121">
					<li>
						<p>The vehicle must be in the <term translate="no">ON</term> position to turn on the headlights.</p>
					</li>
					<li>
						<p>For Europe</p>
						<ul id="e01122">
							<li>
								<p>Even when the light switch is in the <term translate="no">OFF</term> position, the headlights (low beam) automatically turn on when driving at night or in low ambient light. These headlights cannot be turned off manually while driving.</p>
							</li>
							<li>
								<p>The position lamps and tail lamps automatically turn on regardless of the light switch position. However, they can be turned off when the vehicle is in P (Park) or the parking brake is engaged, and the light switch is set to the <term translate="no">OFF</term> position.</p>
							</li>
						</ul>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</note>
			<note type="tip" id="e01123">
			</note>
		</section>
		<section id="e01124">
			<title>Headlight (High Beam) <image href="images/WKIA_046.jpg" scale="15" align="center" placement="inline"/></title>
			<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e01125">
				<tgroup cols="2" colsep="0" rowsep="1">
					<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
					<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
					<tbody>
						<row rowsep="1">
							<entry colname="col1">
								<fig id="e01126">
									<image align="center" placement="break" scale="95" href="images/N_SP327_B05_005.jpg"/>
								</fig>
							</entry>
							<entry colname="col2">
								<fig id="e01127">
									<image align="center" placement="break" scale="95" href="images/N_SP327_B05_004.jpg"/>
								</fig>
							</entry>
						</row>
					</tbody>
				</tgroup>
			</table>
			<ul id="e01128">
				<li>
					<p>To turn on the high beam headlights, push the lever away from you.</p>
					<p>When the high beam headlights are turned on, the lever will return to its original position, and the high beam indicator on the instrument cluster will illuminate.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>To flash the high beam headlamps, pull the lever toward you.</p>
					<p>The lever will return to the normal (low beam) setting when released. The headlight switch does not need to be on to flash the high beam headlights.</p>
				</li>
			</ul>
			<note type="warning" id="e01129">
				<p>High beams</p>
				<p>Do not use the high beam headlight when there are other vehicles in front of or approaching your vehicle, as the light may obstruct the other driver’s vision.</p>
			</note>
		</section>
		<section importance="optional" id="e01130">
			<title>Auto light</title>
			<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e01131">
				<tgroup cols="2" colsep="0" rowsep="1">
					<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
					<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
					<tbody>
						<row rowsep="1">
							<entry colname="col1">
								<fig id="e01132">
									<image align="center" placement="break" scale="95" href="images/N_SP327_B05_006.jpg"/>
								</fig>
							</entry>
							<entry colname="col2"/>
						</row>
					</tbody>
				</tgroup>
			</table>
			<p>When the light switch is in the <term translate="no">AUTO</term> light position, the taillights and headlights will turn on or off automatically depending on the amount of ambient light.</p>
			<sectiondiv><ph>Light switch settings</ph>
				<table outputclass="formatc" frame="all" rowsep="1" colsep="1" id="e01133">
					<tgroup cols="2">
						<colspec colname="c1" colnum="1" colwidth="1*"/>
						<colspec colname="c2" colnum="2" colwidth="1*"/>
						<thead>
							<row>
								<entry>Setting</entry>
								<entry>Result</entry>
							</row>
						</thead>
						<tbody>
							<row>
								<entry>
									<fig id="e01134">
										<title>Position lamp and taillight <image href="images/WKIA_049.jpg" scale="15" align="left" placement="inline"/></title>
										<image href="images/N_SP327_B05_002.jpg" scale="95" align="center" placement="break"/>
									</fig>
								</entry>
								<entry valign="middle">
									<p>Front position lamp, taillights, and license plate lamp are on.</p>
									<note type="tip" id="e01135">
										<p>The vehicle must be in the <term translate="no">ON</term> position to turn on the headlights.</p>
									</note>
								</entry>
							</row>
							<row>
								<entry>
									<fig id="e01136">
										<title>Headlight (low beam) <image href="images/WKIA_047.jpg" scale="15" align="center" placement="inline"/></title>
										<image align="center" placement="break" scale="95" href="images/N_SP327_B05_003.jpg"/>
									</fig>
								</entry>
								<entry valign="middle">
									<p>Low beam headlight, taillight, and license plate lamp are on.</p>
								</entry>
							</row>
							<row>
								<entry>
									<fig id="e01137">
										<title>AUTO light</title>
										<image align="center" placement="break" scale="95" href="images/N_SP327_B05_006.jpg"/>
									</fig>
								</entry>
								<entry valign="middle">
									<p>Taillights and headlights turn on or off automatically depending on the amount of ambient light.</p>
								</entry>
							</row>
						</tbody>
					</tgroup>
				</table>
				<note type="note" id="e01138">
					<ul id="e01139">
						<li>
							<p>For optimal <term translate="no">AUTO</term> light setting performance, never place anything over the sensor (1) located on the instrument panel.</p>
							<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e01140">
								<tgroup cols="2" colsep="0" rowsep="1">
									<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
									<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
									<tbody>
										<row rowsep="1">
											<entry colname="col1">
												<fig id="e01141">
													<image align="center" placement="break" scale="95" href="images/N_SP327_B05_007_1.jpg"/>
												</fig>
											</entry>
											<entry colname="col2"/>
										</row>
									</tbody>
								</tgroup>
							</table>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>Do not clean the sensor with a window cleaner, as it may leave a thin film that could interfere with sensor operation.</p>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>If your vehicle has a window tint or other metallic coating on the front windshield, the <term translate="no">AUTO</term> light system may not work properly.</p>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</note>
			</sectiondiv>
		</section>
	</conbody>
